Return the full /info dictionary for the initial txtAirPlay query.

Older macOS senders (seen with 10.13 High Sierra, AirPlay/366.76.2) send only the
qualified GET /info and close the connection when the reply has nothing but
txtAirPlay.
---
--- a/lib/raop_handlers.h
+++ b/lib/raop_handlers.h
@@ -105,10 +105,8 @@
         plist_dict_set_item(res_node, txtRAOP, txt_raop_node);
     }
   
-    /* don't need anything below here in the response to initial  "txtAirPlay" GET/info request */
-    if (content_type) {
-        goto finished;
-    }
+    /* the initial "txtAirPlay" GET/info request also gets the full info dict: older macOS
+       senders (e.g. 10.13) send no second GET/info and give up without it */
  
     /* deviceID is the physical hardware address, and will not change */
     int hw_addr_raw_len = 0;
